---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { company } from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — UPos" description="How UPos collects, uses, protects and shares personal information.">
  <section class="legal-hero compact"><div class="shell"><p class="kicker"><span></span> Legal</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>Last updated: {company.lastUpdated}</p></div></section>
  <article class="legal-copy shell">
    <p>This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>{company.legalName}</strong> (“UPos”, “we”, “us”) handles personal information when you visit our website, create an account or use the UPos service.</p>
    <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
    <p>We collect account details such as name, work email and organization; service data you submit, including product, store, staff and transaction records; device and usage information such as browser, IP address, timestamps and diagnostics; and support communications. We do not receive or store full payment-card details.</p>
    <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
    <p>We use information to provide and secure the Service, authenticate users, process orders, offer support, maintain business records, prevent fraud, comply with law and improve performance. We send marketing only with a valid legal basis, and you may opt out at any time.</p>
    <h2>3. Legal bases</h2>
    <p>Where applicable, we process information to perform our contract with you, comply with legal obligations, pursue legitimate interests such as security and product improvement, and on the basis of consent where required.</p>
    <h2>4. Payments</h2>
    <p>Paddle acts as Merchant of Record and independently processes information needed to purchase a UPos software subscription, including checkout, payment, tax, invoicing, fraud prevention and buyer support. Review <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/privacy" rel="noreferrer">Paddle’s Privacy Notice</a> for its practices. Paddle shares limited buyer data with us for software access and support. UPos does not receive or store full card details.</p>
    <h2>5. Sharing</h2>
    <p>We share information only with vetted providers that help us host, monitor and support the Service; with professional advisers; when legally required; during a corporate transaction; or with your instruction. Providers may process data only for agreed purposes and under appropriate safeguards. We do not sell personal information.</p>
    <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
    <p>Information may be processed outside your country. Where required, we use recognized safeguards such as adequacy decisions or standard contractual clauses.</p>
    <h2>7. Retention and security</h2>
    <p>We retain information only as long as needed for the purposes above, contractual commitments and legal recordkeeping. We use technical and organizational safeguards including access controls, encryption in transit, backups and monitoring. No system can guarantee absolute security.</p>
    <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on your location, you may request access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability or objection; withdraw consent; and complain to your data-protection authority. We may verify your identity before responding. Contact <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>.</p>
    <h2>9. Cookies</h2>
    <p>We use essential storage needed for security and core site functions. If we introduce non-essential analytics or advertising cookies, we will request consent where required and provide controls before they are set.</p>
    <h2>10. Children</h2>
    <p>The Service is designed for businesses and is not directed to children under 16. We do not knowingly collect their personal information.</p>
    <h2>11. Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>We may update this Policy and will post the new date. Questions or requests can be sent to:<br/>{company.legalName}<br/><a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
